    "done_when": "reckon/schema/flight.yaml declares effective_input_window on a backend beside usable_input_window, with a description that says what it is measured from, and reckon/_flight_schema.py is regenerated with scripts/regen_flight_schema.py rather than edited by hand. The backend settings copy in reckon/crew/routing.py carries the value the same way it carries usable_input_window, so the reader at the context-fit check receives it from a real configuration and not only from a test fixture. No host or repository configuration file sets a value. A new tests/test_effective_window_slot.py loads a flight configuration that declares effective_input_window below usable_input_window, resolves the backend through the production path, and asserts that a prompt estimate between the two is refused by the context-fit check with a reason naming the effective figure, that the same estimate passes when the key is absent, and that a non-integer value is refused at load. The named negative control (drop the key from the settings copy) reddens the refusal case. The gate is tests/test_effective_window_slot.py, tests/test_routing_surface.py, tests/test_flight.py and tests/test_binding_window.py at base and at head. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete, printed and listed in artifacts. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/a-review-dies-where-nobody-is-looking/effective-window-slot.html records the change and states that the value for any backend is a separate configuration decision. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "A backend in flight configuration can declare effective_input_window, the input size its endpoint actually refuses above, so the context-fit check in reckon/crew/routing.py that already reads it gates on the boundary that kills rather than on usable_input_window alone. The slot is declared and carried; no configuration sets a value in this node.",
